course: dictionary
lesson: 13717
title: Doing it without thinking
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some actions happen before you have time to think. Your body just knows what to do. A word for this is instinctively, which means doing something naturally, without thinking about it or being taught. «Sam's hand instinctively pulled away from the hot pan.» Sam did not decide to move his hand. His body did it at once.
explain: Look at the words around instinctively to find its meaning. «Baby turtles hatch on the beach and instinctively head for the sea.» Nobody has taught the turtles the way to the sea, and they do not stop to think about it. The clues are that they hatch, nobody teaches them, and they go straight to the water. Those clues tell you the meaning.
explain: Use the swap check. Try a simple phrase in place of the hard word: «Sam's hand pulled away without thinking.» It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning. Instinctively is often about animals and about quick reactions, but it can describe people too.
fact: Instinctively means doing something naturally, without thinking or being taught.
fact: «Instinctively» comes from the idea of instinct, a feeling or urge you are born with.
fact: Animals act instinctively: birds build nests, spiders spin webs and baby turtles head to the sea without being taught.
fact: People act instinctively in danger: they pull a hand away from heat or put their arms out when they start to fall.
fact: Phrases to remember: «act instinctively» and «know instinctively».
exercise: «Sam instinctively pulled his hand away from the hot pan.» What does instinctively mean here? | *Without thinking, as if the body does it automatically | Slowly, after a long think | With great care and careful planning | Only when someone tells you to
exercise: «The bird knew instinctively how to build a nest.» What does instinctively tell you about the bird? | *It knew how to build a nest without being taught | It did not want a nest | Its mum taught it to build the nest | It built the nest very slowly
exercise: «Mia instinctively ducked when the ball flew at her head.» Why did Mia duck? | She was bored and wanted to move | She had planned it for days | Her coach told her to duck | *Her body reacted before she had time to think
test: «Spiders instinctively spin webs, even if they have never seen one.» What does this sentence show? | *Spiders know how to spin webs without being taught | Spiders only spin webs in winter | Spiders hate webs and avoid them | Spiders learn to spin webs from their parents
test: Which phrase means the same as instinctively? | Reluctantly, against her will | After a long, careful think | *Without thinking, by natural feeling | With a loud voice
exam: «Ella instinctively held the baby bird gently, and she had never been shown how.» What does this tell you about Ella? | She was told exactly what to do by her teacher | She had practised holding birds for years | *She acted naturally, without thinking or being taught | She was frightened and dropped the bird
